<div class="pk5e-root">

  <div class="pk5e-body">
    <div class="pk5e-pane">

      <p class="pk5e-lead">
        Which compendiums the reference window reads. Leave everything unticked
        to read them all.
      </p>
      <p class="pk5e-note">
        Which classes and subclasses appear is decided by what you put in the
        compendium and how you name its folders - folders sharing a name are
        merged across compendiums.
      </p>
      <p class="pk5e-note">
        With "Reference: GM sees every compendium" switched on in the module
        settings, this selection applies to players only.
      </p>

      <div class="pk5e-bulk">
        <input type="search" data-search placeholder="Filter compendiums..." autocomplete="off">
        <button type="button" data-action="selectAll">Select all</button>
        <button type="button" data-action="selectNone">Clear</button>
      </div>

      <p class="pk5e-note" data-summary>
        {{#if usingAll}}
          Nothing selected - all {{total}} compendiums will be read.
        {{else}}
          {{selected}} of {{total}} compendiums selected.
        {{/if}}
      </p>

      <div class="pk5e-packs">
        {{#each packs}}
        <label class="pk5e-pack" data-search="{{search}}">
          <input type="checkbox" data-pack="{{id}}" {{#if checked}}checked{{/if}}>
          <span class="pk5e-pack-name">{{label}}</span>
          <span class="pk5e-pack-origin">{{origin}}</span>
        </label>
        {{/each}}
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>

  <footer class="pk5e-footer">
    <span class="pk5e-hint">Applies to the reference window only.</span>
    <button type="button" class="pk5e-primary" data-action="save">Save</button>
  </footer>

</div>
